Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:25:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: a headless client harness - Xvfb, Mesa lavapipe and
 Fabric Loader around the dev-shadow jar

fetch.py gets the vanilla client, its libraries, the asset objects (not the
sounds) and Fabric Loader's libraries at the versions gradle.properties pins.
run.sh starts the client under Xvfb inside a 2 GB box: -Xmx640m, no Gradle
alive, graphicsPreset pinned to custom and render distance 2. drive.sh clicks,
types into the chat, takes screenshots and makes a superflat world. The README
records what each hazard cost.

Verified from an empty directory with nothing from earlier runs: world created,
#help answered, #goto ~30 ~ ~20 walked to its goal block, no exception.
