+# A Minecraft client with no screen
+
+Runs Minecraft 26.3 with this checkout's Baritone in it, on a machine with no display and no GPU, so a change can be
+walked in a real game instead of only being read. It exists because the first walk in one found a crash that every
+unit test had missed (`PathExecutorBoundsTest` is the record of it).
+
+What is in it: Xvfb for the display, Mesa's software Vulkan (lavapipe) for the renderer, the vanilla client, Fabric
+Loader, and `fabric/build/libs/*-dev-shadow.jar`. Nothing here touches the build or the product.
+
+## What it needs
+
+- Debian or Ubuntu packages: `xvfb libgl1 libgl1-mesa-dri libglx-mesa0 libegl1 mesa-vulkan-drivers libvulkan1 xdotool
+  imagemagick libxrandr2 libxcursor1 libxxf86vm1 libxi6 libxrender1 libxext6 libxtst6 libxinerama1 libxkbcommon0`
+- Java 25 (`JAVA=` if it is not the `java` on the path), and Python 3.
+- Measured on 2 vCPU, 1.9 GB, no swap, Debian 13: with `-Xmx640m` the client is **1.25 to 1.3 GB resident**, runs at
+  about 13 fps (render distance 2, software Vulkan), and the integrated server spends **2.5 of its 50 ms** a tick.
+  A Gradle build (about 1 GB) does not fit beside it: build, stop Gradle, then start the client. `run.sh` refuses to
+  start while Gradle is alive.
+
+## The steps
+
+```
+python3 scripts/headless/fetch.py              # 227 MB, about 4 s; versions come from gradle.properties
+./gradlew :fabric:shadowJar                    # 25-30 s warm; no client running
+scripts/headless/run.sh                        # in the background; the log is $BARITONE_HEADLESS/client.log
+                                               # about 25 s to the title screen
+scripts/headless/drive.sh newworld             # once: a superflat world, commands on, peaceful
+scripts/headless/drive.sh chat '#goto ~30 ~ ~20'
+scripts/headless/drive.sh key F3               # the debug overlay: position, facing, ms per tick
+scripts/headless/drive.sh shot /tmp/a.png 60   # the game window, scaled to 60%
+grep CHAT "$BARITONE_HEADLESS/client.log"      # what Baritone and the game said
+```
+
+`BARITONE_HEADLESS` is where everything lives (default `~/baritone-headless`). Later starts enter the saved world at
+once. The default window is 854x480 on a 1024x600 screen; `drive.sh` clicks at coordinates for exactly that.
+
+## What cost a run each, so it need not again
+
+- **OpenGL does not come up under Xvfb** ("Couldn't find matching GLX visual"). The client falls back to Vulkan by
+  itself; the log says `Using graphics backend Vulkan ... llvmpipe`.
+- **The title screen needs the asset objects**: its panorama is an asset, not part of the jar, and a client without
+  them crashes at the first reload. `fetch.py` takes every object except the sounds.
+- **The first-run screen** ("Would you like to enable the Narrator") takes the first clicks. `run.sh` sets
+  `onboardAccessibility:false`.
+- **A graphics preset puts its own distances back at every start.** A game-written `options.txt` says
+  `graphicsPreset:"fancy"`, which means render distance 16 whatever the file says: the heap fills, the client drops to
+  8 fps and a walk never finishes. `run.sh` pins `graphicsPreset:"custom"`, render distance 2, simulation distance 5.
+- **Slimes spawn on a superflat surface by day** and killed the player 40 seconds into the first run. `newworld` sets
+  peaceful. A player who dies stays dead in the save, and the next start opens on the death screen:
+  `drive.sh respawn`.
+- **A crash in the tick** logs `Unreported exception thrown!`, writes `game/crash-reports/`, and may leave the
+  process alive with a black screen. Count `Unreported`, `IndexOutOfBounds`, `NoClassDefFound`, `MixinApply` in
+  the log after every run.
+- **`T: 20` on the first line of F3 is the frame cap** (`maxFps`), not the tick rate. The server's cost is the
+  `Integrated server @ x/50.0 ms` line on the right of the overlay.
+- The shadow jar does not carry `nether-pathfinder` (only `remapJar` nests it) and Baritone asks for it at start-up,
+  so `run.sh` adds it from the Gradle cache; `fabric/build/libs` can hold several shadow jars, and it takes the newest.
+
+## What it can and cannot see
+
+It shows that the mod loads (every mixin applies), that commands run, and that a path can be walked to its end,
+by position, facing and screenshots. It has **no per-tick record**: nothing here logs keys, yaw or pitch per tick, so
+a rhythm or an angle over time is out of its reach until something writes one. Rendering is software, so frame
+timing says nothing about a real machine; tick timing does.
diff --git a/scripts/headless/drive.sh b/scripts/headless/drive.sh
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..e578ca5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/headless/drive.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+# Drives the headless client the way a person would - the mouse and the keyboard, through xdotool - and reads
+# it the way a person would: screenshots, and the log. The screen is 1024x600 and the game window is 854x480
+# at (85, 60); the coordinates below are on the screen, for a window of that size.
+#
+# usage: drive.sh chat TEXT | key KEY | click X Y | shot FILE [PERCENT] | wait-login | respawn | newworld
+#   chat       opens the chat with t, types TEXT, sends it ('#goto ~30 ~ ~20', '/difficulty peaceful')
+#   shot       the game window, optionally scaled down, as a PNG
+#   newworld   on a fresh game directory only: creates a superflat world with commands on, waits for the
+#              login, and sets the difficulty to peaceful (slimes spawn on a superflat surface by day)
+# environment: BARITONE_HEADLESS (default ~/baritone-headless), HEADLESS_DISPLAY (:99)
+set -eu
+MC_DIR="${BARITONE_HEADLESS:-$HOME/baritone-headless}"
+export DISPLAY="${HEADLESS_DISPLAY:-:99}"
+LOG="$MC_DIR/client.log"
+
+click() { xdotool mousemove "$1" "$2"; sleep 0.4; xdotool click 1; sleep 0.8; }
+chat() { xdotool key t; sleep 1.2; xdotool type --delay 80 -- "$1"; sleep 0.6; xdotool key Return; }
+
+case "${1:-}" in
+    chat) chat "$2" ;;
+    key) xdotool key "$2" ;;
+    click) click "$2" "$3" ;;
+    shot) import -window root png:- | convert png:- -crop 854x480+85+60 +repage -resize "${3:-100}%" "$2" ;;
+    wait-login)
+        for _ in $(seq 1 45); do
+            grep -q 'logged in with entity id' "$LOG" 2>/dev/null && exit 0
+            sleep 2
+        done
+        echo "drive.sh: no login in 90 seconds - see $LOG" >&2
+        exit 1 ;;
+    respawn) click 511 343 ;;
+    newworld)
+        click 511 296   # Singleplayer: with no world saved the game goes straight to Create New World
+        sleep 2
+        click 400 343   # Allow Commands: ON
+        click 512 87    # the World tab
+        click 351 149   # World Type: Superflat
+        click 776 295   # Generate Structures: OFF
+        click 353 507   # Create New World
+        "$0" wait-login
+        sleep 6
+        chat '/difficulty peaceful' ;;
+    *) sed -n '2,12p' "$0"; exit 2 ;;
+esac
diff --git a/scripts/headless/fetch.py b/scripts/headless/fetch.py
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..b939bf7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/headless/fetch.py
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Fetches what a headless Baritone client needs and Gradle does not leave lying around.
+
+  - the vanilla client jar and its Linux libraries, from Mojang's version manifest
+  - the asset index and every asset object except the sounds (the title screen's panorama is an asset;
+    the sounds are not needed and are four fifths of the weight)
+  - the Fabric Loader's libraries, from Fabric's launcher profile
+
+usage: fetch.py [--dir DIR] [--minecraft VERSION] [--loader VERSION]
+
+The versions default to the ones pinned in gradle.properties, DIR to $BARITONE_HEADLESS or
+~/baritone-headless. Mojang's files are checked against the hash they were published with, and files
+that are already there are not fetched again. See README.md in this directory.
+"""
+import argparse
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+import re
+import sys
+import urllib.request
+from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor
+
+REPO = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), '..', '..'))
+MAVEN_CENTRAL = 'https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/'
+
+
+def properties():
+    found = {}
+    with open(os.path.join(REPO, 'gradle.properties')) as f:
+        for line in f:
+            m = re.match(r'^\s*([\w.]+)\s*=\s*(.*?)\s*$', line)
+            if m:
+                found[m.group(1)] = m.group(2)
+    return found
+
+
+def fetch_json(url):
+    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=60) as r:
+        return json.load(r)
+
+
+def on_linux(library):
+    allowed = 'rules' not in library
+    for rule in library.get('rules', []):
+        if rule.get('os', {}).get('name') in (None, 'linux'):
+            allowed = rule['action'] == 'allow'
+    return allowed
+
+
+def download(job):
+    dest, urls, sha1 = job
+    if os.path.exists(dest):
+        if sha1 is None or hashlib.sha1(open(dest, 'rb').read()).hexdigest() == sha1:
+            return 'cached'
+    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dest), exist_ok=True)
+    for url in urls:
+        for _ in range(3):
+            try:
+                with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=60) as r:
+                    data = r.read()
+            except Exception:
+                continue
+            if sha1 is None or hashlib.sha1(data).hexdigest() == sha1:
+                with open(dest, 'wb') as f:
+                    f.write(data)
+                return 'ok'
+    return 'FAILED ' + urls[0]
+
+
+def run(jobs, label):
+    with ThreadPoolExecutor(12) as pool:
+        results = list(pool.map(download, jobs))
+    failed = [r for r in results if r.startswith('FAILED')]
+    print('%-12s %4d files: %d fetched, %d already there, %d failed'
+          % (label, len(results), results.count('ok'), results.count('cached'), len(failed)))
+    if failed:
+        sys.exit('\n'.join(failed[:5]))
+
+
+def main():
+    pins = properties()
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    ap.add_argument('--dir', default=os.environ.get('BARITONE_HEADLESS', os.path.expanduser('~/baritone-headless')))
+    ap.add_argument('--minecraft', default=pins['minecraft_version'])
+    ap.add_argument('--loader', default=pins['fabric_version'])
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+    root = os.path.abspath(args.dir)
+
+    manifest = fetch_json('https://piston-meta.mojang.com/mc/game/version_manifest_v2.json')
+    entry = next((v for v in manifest['versions'] if v['id'] == args.minecraft), None)
+    if entry is None:
+        sys.exit('Minecraft %s is not in the version manifest' % args.minecraft)
+    version = fetch_json(entry['url'])
+
+    client = version['downloads']['client']
+    jobs = [(root + '/client.jar', [client['url']], client['sha1'])]
+    classpath = [root + '/client.jar']
+    for lib in version['libraries']:
+        artifact = lib['downloads'].get('artifact')
+        if artifact and on_linux(lib):
+            dest = root + '/libs/' + artifact['path'].replace('/', '__')
+            jobs.append((dest, [artifact['url']], artifact['sha1']))
+            classpath.append(dest)
+    run(jobs, 'client')
+
+    index = version['assetIndex']
+    index_path = '%s/assets/indexes/%s.json' % (root, index['id'])
+    run([(index_path, [index['url']], index['sha1'])], 'asset index')
+    with open(index_path) as f:
+        objects = json.load(f)['objects']
+    wanted = []
+    for name, obj in objects.items():
+        if not name.endswith('.ogg'):
+            h = obj['hash']
+            wanted.append(('%s/assets/objects/%s/%s' % (root, h[:2], h), ['https://resources.download.minecraft.net/%s/%s' % (h[:2], h)], h))
+    run(wanted, 'assets')
+
+    profile = fetch_json('https://meta.fabricmc.net/v2/versions/loader/%s/%s/profile/json' % (args.minecraft, args.loader))
+    fabric_jobs = []
+    fabric_classpath = []
+    for lib in profile['libraries']:
+        group, artifact, ver = lib['name'].split(':')
+        rel = '%s/%s/%s/%s-%s.jar' % (group.replace('.', '/'), artifact, ver, artifact, ver)
+        dest = '%s/fabric-libs/%s-%s.jar' % (root, artifact, ver)
+        fabric_jobs.append((dest, [lib.get('url', 'https://maven.fabricmc.net/').rstrip('/') + '/' + rel, MAVEN_CENTRAL + rel], None))
+        fabric_classpath.append(dest)
+    run(fabric_jobs, 'fabric')
+
+    for name, text in (('classpath.txt', ':'.join(classpath)), ('fabric-classpath.txt', ':'.join(fabric_classpath)),
+                       ('asset-index.txt', index['id']), ('minecraft-version.txt', args.minecraft)):
+        with open(os.path.join(root, name), 'w') as f:
+            f.write(text)
+    print('ready in', root)
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
diff --git a/scripts/headless/run.sh b/scripts/headless/run.sh
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..f639175d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/headless/run.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+# Starts the Fabric client with the Baritone mod you built, with no screen: Xvfb for the display and Mesa's
+# software Vulkan (lavapipe) for the renderer. OpenGL does not come up under Xvfb ("Couldn't find matching GLX
+# visual"); the client falls back to Vulkan by itself, so nothing here has to ask for it.
+#
+# Needs: fetch.py already run, ./gradlew :fabric:shadowJar already built, and NO Gradle alive - on a 2 GB box
+# the client (about 1.3 GB resident) and a Gradle build (about 1 GB) do not fit together.
+#
+# usage: run.sh [extra game arguments]        the log is $BARITONE_HEADLESS/client.log
+# environment: BARITONE_HEADLESS (default ~/baritone-headless), HEADLESS_DISPLAY (:99), HEADLESS_WORLD
+#   ("New World": entered at once if it exists), HEADLESS_HEAP (640m), HEADLESS_USER, JAVA (java, 25 or later)
+set -eu
+REPO="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)"
+MC_DIR="${BARITONE_HEADLESS:-$HOME/baritone-headless}"
+DISPLAY_NAME="${HEADLESS_DISPLAY:-:99}"
+WORLD="${HEADLESS_WORLD:-New World}"
+JAVA="${JAVA:-java}"
+
+for f in classpath.txt fabric-classpath.txt asset-index.txt minecraft-version.txt; do
+    [ -f "$MC_DIR/$f" ] || { echo "run.sh: $MC_DIR/$f is missing - run scripts/headless/fetch.py first" >&2; exit 1; }
+done
+MOD="$(ls -t "$REPO"/fabric/build/libs/*-dev-shadow.jar 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)"
+[ -n "$MOD" ] || { echo "run.sh: no fabric/build/libs/*-dev-shadow.jar - run ./gradlew :fabric:shadowJar first" >&2; exit 1; }
+# the shadow jar does not carry nether-pathfinder (only remapJar nests it), and Baritone asks for it at start-up
+NETHER="$(find "${GRADLE_USER_HOME:-$HOME/.gradle}/caches/modules-2/files-2.1/dev.babbaj/nether-pathfinder" -name 'nether-pathfinder-*.jar' ! -name '*-sources.jar' 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)"
+[ -n "$NETHER" ] || { echo "run.sh: nether-pathfinder is not in the Gradle cache - build once first" >&2; exit 1; }
+if pgrep -f 'gradlew|GradleWrapperMain|GradleDaemon|gradle-launcher' >/dev/null; then
+    echo "run.sh: Gradle is running; the client will not fit beside it" >&2
+    exit 1
+fi
+
+export DISPLAY="$DISPLAY_NAME"
+export LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1
+export LP_NUM_THREADS=1
+mkdir -p "$MC_DIR/natives/lwjgl" "$MC_DIR/natives/jna" "$MC_DIR/natives/netty" "$MC_DIR/natives/java" "$MC_DIR/game/mods"
+pgrep -x Xvfb >/dev/null || { Xvfb "$DISPLAY_NAME" -screen 0 1024x600x24 +extension GLX +render -noreset >"$MC_DIR/xvfb.log" 2>&1 & sleep 2; }
+cp -f "$MOD" "$MC_DIR/game/mods/baritone.jar"
+
+# Set on every start: the first-run screen asks about the narrator and would take the first clicks, and the
+# rest keeps the client inside a 2 GB box. Edit them in game/options.txt only if you also change this.
+OPTIONS="$MC_DIR/game/options.txt"
+touch "$OPTIONS"
+set_option() { # key value
+    if grep -q "^$1:" "$OPTIONS"; then sed -i "s|^$1:.*|$1:$2|" "$OPTIONS"; else echo "$1:$2" >> "$OPTIONS"; fi
+}
+set_option onboardAccessibility false
+set_option skipMultiplayerWarning true
+set_option preferredGraphicsBackend '"vulkan"'
+set_option graphicsPreset '"custom"' # a preset puts its own render and simulation distance back at every start
+set_option renderDistance 2
+set_option simulationDistance 5
+set_option maxFps 20
+set_option soundCategory_master 0.0
+set_option tutorialStep '"none"'
+
+QUICKPLAY=()
+[ -d "$MC_DIR/game/saves/$WORLD" ] && QUICKPLAY=(--quickPlaySingleplayer "$WORLD")
+cd "$MC_DIR/game"
+exec "$JAVA" -Xmx"${HEADLESS_HEAP:-640m}" -Xms96m -XX:+UseSerialGC -XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1 \
+    -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=192m -XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=64m -XX:StackShadowPages=32 \
+    --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED --add-exports java.base/jdk.internal.misc=ALL-UNNAMED \
+    -Djava.library.path="$MC_DIR/natives/java" \
+    -Dorg.lwjgl.system.SharedLibraryExtractPath="$MC_DIR/natives/lwjgl" \
+    -Djna.tmpdir="$MC_DIR/natives/jna" -Dio.netty.native.workdir="$MC_DIR/natives/netty" \
+    "-DFabricMcEmu= net.minecraft.client.main.Main " \
+    -cp "$(cat "$MC_DIR/fabric-classpath.txt"):$(cat "$MC_DIR/classpath.txt"):$NETHER" \
+    net.fabricmc.loader.impl.launch.knot.KnotClient \
+    --username "${HEADLESS_USER:-Headless}" --version "$(cat "$MC_DIR/minecraft-version.txt")" \
+    --gameDir "$MC_DIR/game" --assetsDir "$MC_DIR/assets" --assetIndex "$(cat "$MC_DIR/asset-index.txt")" \
+    --uuid 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 --accessToken 0 --versionType release \
+    --width 854 --height 480 ${QUICKPLAY[@]+"${QUICKPLAY[@]}"} "$@" >"$MC_DIR/client.log" 2>&1
